{**
 * c-scrollspy - the contents of a long page, which marks the part of the page
 * being read.
 *
 * It is a navigation, named, holding a c-list-group of links to places on the
 * same page (#id), and without the script that is all it is: a list of
 * contents that works. assets/scrollspy.ts watches the places the links lead
 * to and marks the entry of the one being read with aria-current="location" -
 * the value for "where you are within the page", as against "page", the page
 * itself. c-list-group already draws an entry that carries aria-current as
 * the one that is on, so nothing about how it looks is new.
 *
 * A place counts as being read once its top has come up into the upper quarter
 * of the part of the window the theme's chrome leaves free - measured from the
 * lower edge of whatever is held over the content (--layout-chrome-offset),
 * where a jump to it stops. The server marks no entry: it cannot know how far
 * the page is scrolled.
 *
 * It stays in view beside the content it lists while that content scrolls,
 * under the held chrome. That is only for a contents placed beside the
 * content, in a column of its own: put above the content in one column, it
 * would ride over the text it lists.
 *
 * @param list<Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\ListGroupItem> $items one entry for each
 *     place, each with an address of the form #id
 *}

{import 'list-group.latte'}

{define scrollspy, string $label, array $items, ?string $testId = null}
    <nav class="c-scrollspy" aria-label="{$label}" data-testid="{$testId}">
        {include listGroup, items: $items}
    </nav>
{/define}
